//------------------------------------------------
//--- 010 Editor v13.0 Binary Template
//
//      File: KeeperFX_SAV.bt
//    Author: jomalin (from KeeperKlan forum https://keeperklan.com/)
//   Version: 1.1
//   Purpose: Parse savegame SAV files (fx1g000X.sav) from KeeperFX videogame ver 0.4.9.2762
//  Category: Game
// File Mask: fx1g*.sav
//   History:  
//   1.1   2022-09-15 jomalin: Add RequiresVersion, clarify some messages and show expected savegame file size in case of error
//   1.0   2022-09-15 jomalin: Initial release.
//------------------------------------------------

/*
IMPORTANT NOTE: This binary template is exactly for KeeperFX 0.4.9.2762 version, it can't be used for any other KeeperFX version that makes
the savegame file be bigger in size (some new versions add more info to it so the file size change), in this case, this code will detect it
and you will see in the Output pane an error like this:
"BLOCKNAME block is INCORRECT..." (where BLOCKNAME is the current block being parsed).
Of course, KeeperFX savegame format is different from the original Dungeon Keeper one.

The process to make this binary template has been:
Being the KeeperFX repository here: https://github.com/dkfans/keeperfx
- Start to read what the load game does:
  https://github.com/dkfans/keeperfx/blob/master/src/game_saves.c
- Copy all defines and structs from the source code that are used from game_saves.c (recursively)
- Replace all syntax that 010 Editor scripting language doesn't understand (*)
- Take care about pragma pack preprocessor directives (makes structs be bigger in size as expected) so add the necessary padding bytes (*)(*)
- All the code comments i added here starts with: "010 Editor note"

(*) These are all the generic kind of comments i have written in this code in the structs, unions or variables to make it work for this
scripting language (very similar to C):
- 010 Editor note: pointer syntax is not supported, changed to use my anyPointer typedef
- 010 Editor note: structs and unions must have a name, we add one
- 010 Editor note: multi-dimensional arrays are not supported, we change it to a struct (workaround proposed on the 010 Editor manual)
- 010 Editor note: this throws "Invalid array size in typedef". Typedefs do not support an expression for an array size, they said to me they will add this on a future version
- 010 Editor note: hardcode value needed as typedefs do not support an expression for an array size
There are only a few other comments, more specific ones.

(*)(*) As KeeperFX uses this preprocessor directive in some parts of the code:
#pragma pack()
some structs are bigger in size as they have padding bytes added between some of its members.
This comment reflects all the places where the padding was necessary here:
- 010 Editor note: necessary padding
More info about alignment and structure packing here:
http://www.catb.org/esr/structure-packing/
https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/is-sizeof-for-a-struct-equal-to-the-sum-of-sizeof-of-each-member/
Keep in mind that every compiler can have its own alignment/packing algorithm, so adding padding bytes must be done in the same place where
the original compiler supposed to added them.
010 Editor will support pragma pack directive in the future, so this tedious process will be avoided someday adding that directive to the
corresponding structs and keeping them clear (without the specific padding bytes).
Some structs that have pragma pack enabled in the KeeperFX source code are:
DoorConfigStats
TrapConfigStats
ManufactureData
TrapDoorConfig
ObjectConfigStats
ObjectsConfig
CreatureModelConfig
CreatureJobConfig
CreatureConfig
TrapInfo
BoxInfo
Coord3d
ComputerEvent
ComputerCheck
ComputerInfo
DungeonAdd
RoomSpace
Take care about them if they change in the future or a new savegame version support want to be added, as padding bytes can be necessary to
be added to parse them.

TO-DO in this binary template in future versions:
- Use InputRadioButtonBox function (requires 010 Editor v5.0 or higher) to select which KeeperFX savegame version is going to be read to
  appropriately parse it.
  This will allow open different savegame version files, not only from 0.4.9.2672.
  "Ifs" must be used on structs to add or not certain members depending on version.
- Add comments to the "Comment" column in the Template results windows with relevant or summarized data:
  https://www.sweetscape.com/010editor/manual/TemplateVariables.htm#VarComments
*/

RequiresVersion(4); //For SPrintf and variable comments
LittleEndian();

